  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Sunday)\nIssued at 942 AM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nMean western NOAM ridging will support mild and dry weather into \nnext week as Pac flow continues aloft. Weak/skirting impulses will\nsupport cool fronts at times to knock temps down a few degrees \nand support passing breezy days. Temps will be above normal in the\nperiod. Departing cool front has knocked temps down 10 to 15 \ndegrees for today, but still mild and above normal with highs in \nthe 50s/60s. The next system will move into the region tomorrow \nwith warmer temps expected per frontside SW flow. This system will\nforce another trough through the region, with breezy NW winds \nexpected by afternoon. A few gusts over 40 mph can be expected esp\non the NW SD Plains and into the lee of the Black Hills. A back \ndoor cool front will slide into the region later Wed, which will \nknock down temps across the SD Plains Thur, esp toward central SD.\nHowever, any cool down will be short lived as the western NOAM \nridge quickly rebuilds into the region, supporting a very mild and\ndry weekend with mild weather continuing into next week.",
